A||||7||Fat Frank||Head Light Motor  88 GT||||5||
Z||000000||Fat Frank||11-14-2001||08:00 AM||||HI everyone. I Have been reading the posts on this site for a while now,and found it to be very friendly as well as informative.So I decided to join up. I just bought an 88 GT with 2.8 Auto and had some trouble with the right headlight not lifting when the lights are turned on. After some info on some posts I pulled the motor and opened the gear case.I had to remove the motor to get the plastic gear out and then when I pulled the gear off the shaft I got a handfull of ground up plastic. My question is where can I get the three plastic cylinders that go under the gear? I found a hot melt glue stick that was about the right size and put it back together and it works. But I don't know how long it will last. Also when I pulled the motor out,the brushes were a problem to hold in place while I put it back together.||||reg||5
Z||000001||skitime||11-14-2001||08:04 AM||||First I want to welcome you to the forum.  We have two 88 GTs and I am sure you will love yours.  Here is where you can go to get the parts you need.  It is an easy fix and you already did most of the work.  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||California Kid||11-14-2001||09:57 AM||||Welcome to the Forum Frank!<P>Skitime lead you to the right place...Rodney is great to deal with, his parts are excellent, and very fairly priced.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||11-14-2001||12:53 PM||||To hold the brushes in place while reassembling the motor, I use 2 paper clips (one for each brush), each bent into a right-angled, planar "?" shape.  The hook end of the "?" holds the brush, the bottom (stem) of the "?" acts as a handle that sticks out.<BR>I clip the brushes into place, and assemble the motor leaving a little (paper clip thickness) gap.  Rotate the clips off the brushes and slide them out, then finish assembling the motor.  <P>Boy, that was hard to describe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">!  I bet Rodney's kit has better instructions than my ramble  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||11-14-2001||03:35 PM||||The glue stick will do it for some time depending how hot the area gets. Maybe during winter it will last. I did it once but I melted the glue to take the shape. After about 1-2 months it failed again. Get Rodney's and do it right.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
