Z||000007||tgowens||11-15-2001||01:10 AM||||but......... you don't have to dis-assemble the motor to remove the gear to install the bushings..... just remove the three 1/4" screws from the side plate, pull the gear out and place the bushings in the detents inside the plastic gear and reassemble -- don't need to open the motor housing at all. You <I>will</I> find that the right side (passenger) is a little different from the left side though -- takes just a little more work..... and yes, Rodney's kit contains very good instructions.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
